# LabelLens — Detailed Implementation Plan
## Smart Compliance Verification System for Packaged Commodities
**SIH 2026 | PS 26034 | Ministry of Consumer Affairs, Food & Public Distribution**

---

## Background

Two files exist today:

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| [label_lens_framework.md](file:///Users/shvetadeshmukh/Desktop/Rutu/SIH/label_lens_framework.md) | Architecture & framework document — defines five pipeline stages, the tech stack, the LMPC rule-engine JSON schema, and system impact metrics |
| [Rule6Prototype.jsx](file:///Users/shvetadeshmukh/Desktop/Rutu/SIH/Rule6Prototype.jsx) | A polished 902-line React prototype — demonstrates Rule 6 logic across three scenarios (physical label, QR-assisted electronics label, e-commerce listing) with animated scanning UI, per-field confidence bars, verdict stamps, and IBM Plex typography |

The task is to build the **full production LabelLens system** that operationalises everything described in the framework document, using the prototype as the starting UI for the analytics portal.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Scope decision needed** — The framework describes a mobile app (React Native / Flutter), a Next.js analytics portal, and a FastAPI backend with three AI microservices. For the SIH hackathon demo, do you want:
>
> **Option A — Full monorepo (recommended):** All components built, with mock AI responses where GPU inference isn't possible locally.  
> **Option B — Portal + API only:** Skip the mobile app; focus on the Next.js dashboard + FastAPI + rule engine.
>
> The plan below assumes **Option A**. Please confirm or adjust before execution starts.

> [!WARNING]
> **AI model weights** — YOLOv8 and PaddleOCR models will be downloaded at setup time (~500 MB combined). An internet connection is required on first run.

