## Proposed Changes

### Monorepo Root

#### [NEW] Monorepo scaffold

```
SIH/
├── apps/
│   ├── portal/          # Next.js 14 analytics dashboard
│   ├── mobile/          # React Native (Expo) field scanner
│   └── api/             # FastAPI orchestration backend
├── services/
│   ├── vision/          # YOLOv8 spatial detection microservice
│   ├── ocr/             # PaddleOCR bilingual extraction microservice
│   └── nlp/             # Semantic NLP/LLM analysis microservice
├── packages/
│   ├── rule-engine/     # Shared Python LMPC rule config + validator
│   └── shared-ui/       # Shared React component library (LogoMark, ConfidenceBar, etc.)
├── data/
│   └── lmpc_rules_v1.json   # Already specified in framework doc
├── docker-compose.yml   # Orchestrates all services locally
└── README.md
```

---

### Component 1 — Rule Engine (`packages/rule-engine/`)

The heart of the system. Every other component calls into this.

#### [NEW] `lmpc_rules_v1.json`

Expanded from the schema in the framework doc to cover all LMPC 2011 rules relevant to the hackathon:

```json
{
  "rule_engine_version": "1.0.4",
  "last_updated": "2026-09-04",
  "applicable_legislation": "Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules, 2011",
  "weight_slabs_font_mapping": [
    { "slab_id": "SLAB_A", "net_quantity_range": {"min_inclusive_g_ml": 0,   "max_inclusive_g_ml": 50},   "mandatory_min_font_height_mm": 1.0 },
    { "slab_id": "SLAB_B", "net_quantity_range": {"min_exclusive_g_ml": 50,  "max_inclusive_g_ml": 200},  "mandatory_min_font_height_mm": 2.0 },
    { "slab_id": "SLAB_C", "net_quantity_range": {"min_exclusive_g_ml": 200, "max_inclusive_g_ml": 1000}, "mandatory_min_font_height_mm": 4.0 },
    { "slab_id": "SLAB_D", "net_quantity_range": {"min_exclusive_g_ml": 1000,"max_inclusive_g_ml": 99999},"mandatory_min_font_height_mm": 6.0 }
  ],
  "mandatory_fields_physical": ["manufacturer_name_address","generic_name","net_quantity","manufacture_date","mrp","consumer_care"],
  "mandatory_fields_ecommerce": ["manufacturer_name_address","generic_name","net_quantity","manufacture_date","mrp","consumer_care","country_of_origin"],
  "qr_offloadable_fields_electronics": ["manufacturer_address","generic_name","dimensions"],
  "prohibited_expressions": ["net weight when packed","approximate weight","approx","gms","kilos","net wt when packed"],
  "mandatory_consumer_care_fields": ["telephone","email","address","name"],
  "confidence_thresholds": { "auto_pass": 85, "auto_fail": 40, "human_review": 75 }
}
```

#### [NEW] `validator.py`

Core Python class that:
1. Loads `lmpc_rules_v1.json`
2. Accepts a structured `ScanResult` dict (fields extracted by OCR/NLP)
3. Resolves the correct font-size slab from net-quantity value
4. Checks field presence, font size compliance, confidence thresholds, prohibited expressions
5. Returns a `ComplianceReport` with per-field verdicts and an overall `pass | review | fail`

---

### Component 2 — Vision Microservice (`services/vision/`)

**Tech:** Python + Ultralytics YOLOv8 + OpenCV + FastAPI

#### [NEW] `main.py` — Vision service entrypoint

Exposes `POST /detect` accepting a multipart image upload. Returns a JSON payload:

```json
{
  "package_type": "physical | ecommerce",
  "is_electronic": true,
  "qr_detected": true,
  "bounding_boxes": {
    "principal_display_panel": [x1, y1, x2, y2],
    "mrp_block": [...],
    "net_quantity_area": [...],
    "consumer_care_block": [...]
  },
  "placement_violations": ["net_quantity_on_secondary_face"],
  "flattened_image_b64": "..."
}
```

#### [NEW] `model.py` — YOLOv8 wrapper

- Downloads `yolov8n.pt` on first load (or a fine-tuned checkpoint if available)
- Fine-tuning note: for the hackathon demo, we use zero-shot detection on the standard YOLOv8 model and supplement with rule-based heuristics. A fine-tuning script on a labelled packaging dataset will be included as a future-state artefact.

#### [NEW] `flattener.py` — 3D-to-2D label flattener

- Uses OpenCV `getPerspectiveTransform` + `warpPerspective` for flat labels
- For cylindrical containers: stitches overlapping keyframe images using `cv2.Stitcher`
- Outputs a flat 2D canvas image as Base64

---

### Component 3 — OCR Microservice (`services/ocr/`)

**Tech:** Python + PaddleOCR + FastAPI

#### [NEW] `main.py` — OCR service entrypoint

Exposes `POST /extract`, accepts Base64 image. Returns:

```json
{
  "fields": [
    {
      "label": "net_quantity",
      "raw_text": "200 g",
      "confidence": 96.4,
      "bounding_box": [x1, y1, x2, y2],
      "font_height_px": 28.5,
      "font_height_mm": 3.9,
      "script": "latin"
    }
  ],
  "pixel_per_mm_ratio": 7.31,
  "calibration_method": "reference_coin | user_supplied_dimension | estimated"
}
```

#### [NEW] `calibrator.py` — Pixel-to-mm ratio calculator

- Strategy 1: detects an Indian 5-rupee coin (known diameter = 23 mm) using shape matching
- Strategy 2: accepts a single user-supplied physical dimension at scan time
- Strategy 3: falls back to heuristic estimation from standard label sizes

#### [NEW] `extractor.py` — PaddleOCR wrapper

- Uses `paddleocr.PaddleOCR(lang='en')` (also loads Hindi/Devanagari model)
- Maps raw OCR text to semantic field labels via regex + heuristics (e.g., `₹` prefix → MRP field)
- Calculates bounding-box height in pixels → converts to mm via calibration ratio

---

### Component 4 — NLP Microservice (`services/nlp/`)

**Tech:** Python + `transformers` (DistilBERT or GPT-4o-mini via API) + FastAPI

#### [NEW] `main.py` — NLP service entrypoint

Exposes `POST /analyze`. Accepts structured field text. Returns:

```json
{
  "prohibited_expressions_found": ["gms"],
  "semantic_contradictions": [
    {"headline": "MRP inclusive of all taxes", "footnote": "*local taxes extra", "severity": "high"}
  ],
  "missing_consumer_care_fields": ["email"],
  "overall_semantic_verdict": "fail"
}
```

#### [NEW] `classifier.py`

- Regex-first pass for prohibited expressions from `lmpc_rules_v1.json`
- LLM pass (GPT-4o-mini or local DistilBERT) for contradiction detection
- Fields checked against `mandatory_consumer_care_fields` list from rule config

---

### Component 5 — FastAPI Orchestration Backend (`apps/api/`)

**Tech:** Python + FastAPI + PostgreSQL (via SQLAlchemy) + AWS S3 / MinIO (via `boto3`)

#### [NEW] `main.py`

Top-level FastAPI app. Key endpoints:

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/scan` | Orchestrates Vision → OCR → NLP → Rule Engine. Returns `ComplianceReport`. |
| `GET` | `/reports/{id}` | Fetch a stored compliance report |
| `GET` | `/reports` | List reports (with filters: date, product, verdict) |
| `POST` | `/reports/{id}/notice` | Generate a Show-Cause Notice PDF |
| `GET` | `/heatmap` | Returns geo-aggregated violation data for dashboard |
| `POST` | `/ecommerce/scrape` | Trigger e-commerce listing scrape by URL |
| `GET` | `/rules` | Returns current lmpc_rules_v1.json (admin) |
| `PUT` | `/rules` | Update rule config without redeploy (admin) |

#### [NEW] `models.py` — SQLAlchemy ORM models

```python
class ScanRecord:
    id: UUID
    product_name: str
    scan_timestamp: datetime
    gps_lat: float
    gps_lng: float
    image_hash_sha256: str  # Chain of custody
    device_id: str
    verdict: Literal["pass", "review", "fail"]
    confidence_composite: float
    report_json: JSON

class ViolationField:
    scan_id: UUID
    field_label: str
    rule_citation: str
    status: Literal["ok", "review", "fail"]
    extracted_value: str
    confidence: float
```

#### [NEW] `evidence_sealer.py` — Chain-of-Custody module

- At image capture: computes `SHA-256` hash of raw bytes
- Appends GPS coordinates, network timestamp (NTP), device hardware ID
- Writes sealed metadata to an immutable log table (append-only via SQL trigger)

#### [NEW] `notice_generator.py` — Show-Cause Notice PDF

- Uses **WeasyPrint** to render an HTML template → PDF
- Template includes: product photo (embedded), violation table, rule citations, inspector signature block, SHA-256 hash watermark
- Output stored in S3/MinIO; presigned URL returned to caller

#### [NEW] `scraper.py` — E-Commerce Compliance Scraper

- Uses `playwright` (headless Chromium) to scrape product listing pages
- Flattens dynamic dropdowns and carousels to extract Rule 6(10) fields
- Checks Rule 6(10A) — country-of-origin filter presence
- Feeds extracted data directly into the rule engine (no OCR stage needed)

